{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"grep -n '\"'^func .*'\"\\\\(Advance\\\\|ApplyConfChange\\\\|Campaign\\\\|ReadIndex\\\\|Status\\\\)' ../agent-source/node.go; nl -ba ../agent-source/node.go | sed -n '470,505p;555,620p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/rawnode.go | sed -n '30,35p'\"","aggregated_output":"472:func (n *node) Campaign(ctx context.Context) error { return n.step(ctx, pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgHup}) }\n554:func (n *node) Advance() {\n561:func (n *node) ApplyConfChange(cc pb.ConfChangeI) *pb.ConfState {\n574:func (n *node) Status() Status {\n591:func (n *node) ReportSnapshot(id uint64, status SnapshotStatus) {\n613:func (n *node) ReadIndex(ctx context.Context, rctx []byte) error {\n   470\t}\n   471\t\n   472\tfunc (n *node) Campaign(ctx context.Context) error { return n.step(ctx, pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgHup}) }\n   473\t\n   474\tfunc (n *node) Propose(ctx context.Context, data []byte) error {\n   475\t\treturn n.stepWait(ctx, pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgProp, Entries: []pb.Entry{{Data: data}}})\n   476\t}\n   477\t\n   478\tfunc (n *node) Step(ctx context.Context, m pb.Message) error {\n   479\t\t// Ignore unexpected local messages receiving over network.\n   480\t\tif IsLocalMsg(m.Type) && !IsLocalMsgTarget(m.From) {\n   481\t\t\t// TODO: return an error?\n   482\t\t\treturn nil\n   483\t\t}\n   484\t\treturn n.step(ctx, m)\n   485\t}\n   486\t\n   487\tfunc confChangeToMsg(c pb.ConfChangeI) (pb.Message, error) {\n   488\t\ttyp, data, err := pb.MarshalConfChange(c)\n   489\t\tif err != nil {\n   490\t\t\treturn pb.Message{}, err\n   491\t\t}\n   492\t\treturn pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgProp, Entries: []pb.Entry{{Type: typ, Data: data}}}, nil\n   493\t}\n   494\t\n   495\tfunc (n *node) ProposeConfChange(ctx context.Context, cc pb.ConfChangeI) error {\n   496\t\tmsg, err := confChangeToMsg(cc)\n   497\t\tif err != nil {\n   498\t\t\treturn err\n   499\t\t}\n   500\t\treturn n.Step(ctx, msg)\n   501\t}\n   502\t\n   503\tfunc (n *node) step(ctx context.Context, m pb.Message) error {\n   504\t\treturn n.stepWithWaitOption(ctx, m, false)\n   505\t}\n   555\t\tselect {\n   556\t\tcase n.advancec <- struct{}{}:\n   557\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   558\t\t}\n   559\t}\n   560\t\n   561\tfunc (n *node) ApplyConfChange(cc pb.ConfChangeI) *pb.ConfState {\n   562\t\tvar cs pb.ConfState\n   563\t\tselect {\n   564\t\tcase n.confc <- cc.AsV2():\n   565\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   566\t\t}\n   567\t\tselect {\n   568\t\tcase cs = <-n.confstatec:\n   569\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   570\t\t}\n   571\t\treturn &cs\n   572\t}\n   573\t\n   574\tfunc (n *node) Status() Status {\n   575\t\tc := make(chan Status)\n   576\t\tselect {\n   577\t\tcase n.status <- c:\n   578\t\t\treturn <-c\n   579\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   580\t\t\treturn Status{}\n   581\t\t}\n   582\t}\n   583\t\n   584\tfunc (n *node) ReportUnreachable(id uint64) {\n   585\t\tselect {\n   586\t\tcase n.recvc <- pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgUnreachable, From: id}:\n   587\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   588\t\t}\n   589\t}\n   590\t\n   591\tfunc (n *node) ReportSnapshot(id uint64, status SnapshotStatus) {\n   592\t\trej := status == SnapshotFailure\n   593\t\n   594\t\tselect {\n   595\t\tcase n.recvc <- pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgSnapStatus, From: id, Reject: rej}:\n   596\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   597\t\t}\n   598\t}\n   599\t\n   600\tfunc (n *node) TransferLeadership(ctx context.Context, lead, transferee uint64) {\n   601\t\tselect {\n   602\t\t// manually set 'from' and 'to', so that leader can voluntarily transfers its leadership\n   603\t\tcase n.recvc <- pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgTransferLeader, From: transferee, To: lead}:\n   604\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   605\t\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n   606\t\t}\n   607\t}\n   608\t\n   609\tfunc (n *node) ForgetLeader(ctx context.Context) error {\n   610\t\treturn n.step(ctx, pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgForgetLeader})\n   611\t}\n   612\t\n   613\tfunc (n *node) ReadIndex(ctx context.Context, rctx []byte) error {\n   614\t\treturn n.step(ctx, pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgReadIndex, Entries: []pb.Entry{{Data: rctx}}})\n   615\t}\n    30\t\n    31\t// RawNode is a thread-unsafe Node.\n    32\t// The methods of this struct correspond to the methods of Node and are described\n    33\t// more fully there.\n    34\ttype RawNode struct {\n    35\t\traft               *raft\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\nnewsrc=[dict(id='node-early-advance',file='node.go',start_line=158,end_line=187,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='doc-early-advance',file='doc.go',start_line=93,end_line=103,kind='document_statement'),dict(id='node-control-methods',file='node.go',start_line=554,end_line=581,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='pending-read-intent',file='raft.go',start_line=428,end_line=432,kind='document_statement'),dict(id='campaign-config-test',file='raft_test.go',start_line=3593,end_line=3668,kind='test_expectation')]\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-entry':\n  b['source_ids']+=['node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','node-control-methods']\n  b['important_branches'].append('Synchronous Node.Advance is explicitly permitted before command application finishes; Node.run invokes RawNode.Advance, whose queued application response advances reported applied progress. Committed application must retain Ready order. This permission is not the async storage-response contract.')\n  b['cross_activity_effects']={'A2':'Early synchronous Advance can advance the reported applied boundary consumed by the campaign configuration scan before deferred application work finishes.'}\n if b['id']=='B-campaign':\n  b['source_ids']+=['node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','node-control-methods','advance','step-vote','campaign-config-test']\n  b['existing_protections'].append('hasUnappliedConfChanges scans (reported applied, committed]; with configuration activation completed before reporting application, previously committed changes block a new campaign until processed. Existing tests assert that guard for timeout and transfer.')\n  b['unknowns']=['With the documented synchronous early-Advance optimization, can reported application hide a deferred committed configuration change from the guard while a later election completes?']\n if b['id']=='B-read':\n  b['source_ids']+=['node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','pending-read-intent','campaign']\n  b['unknowns']=['Can a synchronous Node caller use documented early Advance, defer a committed configuration activation, elect that node under its old active config, queue ReadIndex before the first current-term commit, then activate the delayed config so switchToConfig advances commitment without releasing the pending request?']\nfor surface in m['surfaces']:\n if surface['entry_point']=='raft.switchToConfig -> maybeCommit':\n  surface['reason']='Source protection narrows reachability: faithful applied progress blocks campaigning with a committed unapplied config, and normal leader commit releases pending reads before later config application. However Node explicitly permits synchronous Advance before application finishes. Whether that permission permits delayed configuration activation across an election is the remaining concrete entry-specific premise; no liveness violation is established.'\n  surface['source_ids']+=['campaign','node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','advance','step-vote']\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation']+=' The synchronous Node API permits early Advance before command application finishes; its reported applied boundary can therefore precede completion of embedding work. The campaign scan reads that reported boundary. Asynchronous apply responses instead follow completed work under their separate contract.'\nm['core_overview']['connection']['source_ids']+=['node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','advance','step-vote','campaign']\nm['core_overview']['open_details']=[('Synchronous early-Advance permission and delayed configuration activation across an election require a legal-history discriminator for the pending-read release lead.' if 'read-release' in x else x) for x in m['core_overview']['open_details']]\njson.dump(m,open('core-map-v1-refined.json','w'),indent=2)\npreserve='The existing storage-qualified commitment obligation/check used AsyncStorageWrites and completed configuration application before response. It did not use synchronous Advance or change membership during its proposal; its meaning, dependencies and observations are preserved.'\nchanges={i:dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','campaign','advance','step-vote'],rationale=why,preserves=preserve) for i,why in {'B-entry':'Record a documented synchronous caller scheduling permission and the actual bookkeeping handoff.','B-campaign':'Clarify that its known scan uses reported applied, not independent observation of completed embedding configuration work.','B-read':'Narrow the existing unresolved release reachability premise to documented early Advance and delayed activation.'}.items()}\ns=dict(action='research',rationale='Retain both the source protection and the synchronous caller permission that prevents closing the pending-read lead by assuming applied always means finished embedding work.',map_path='core-map-v1-refined.json',map_changes=changes,sources=newsrc,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['campaign','node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','node-control-methods','advance','step-vote','config-activate','pending-read-intent','campaign-config-test'],answered='Source observation: hup refuses to campaign while a committed configuration change lies above reported applied; candidates receiving append/heartbeat/snapshot become followers, so ordinary received commitment cannot silently install a new prefix while preserving candidacy. Existing tests expect the campaign and transfer guard, but those tests are not new execution evidence. Inference under faithful completed-application reporting: delayed old-term configuration changes block becoming leader, while configuration committed by the current leader normally follows a current-term commit that already releases pending reads. Contrary interface evidence prevents general closure: Node.Advance explicitly permits finishing Ready before command application completes, and doc.go allows Advance at any point after persistence with application order preserved. Node.run -> RawNode.Advance -> MsgStorageApplyResp advances the reported applied index used by the guard. Therefore the missing release call must be assessed against this entry-specific scheduling permission, not only the guard. Async storage responses have a different completed-work contract.',remaining=['Determine actual same-execution reachability using synchronous Node: persist and early-Advance a committed membership reduction, defer its application, elect the node, queue a read, then apply the saved change.','Determine whether reducing a four-voter majority to a three-voter majority can make configuration activation the first current-term commit event while pending reads remain.','If reachable, distinguish a bounded internal release obligation from eventual externally completed read service; a finite timeout alone would not establish general liveness failure.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Next use a small clean-copy exploration with the public Node API, actual produced messages and FIFO application batches. It will test the limiting legal-history premise before spending an obligation on an unproven liveness interpretation. A four-to-three voter reduction changes threshold from three to two; preserving a delayed application batch while allowing only two replicas to append the new-term entry makes the config activation effect discriminating.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_10-41-34-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
